{"availability":"available","full":"varn-org/varn","name":"varn","description":"Lua everywhere. Write the application once in Lua and run that same code on desktop, mobile and in the browser, on a C++ core that already brings everything it needs.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C++","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-01T02:29:50Z","updated":"2026-10-06T04:28:09Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://varn.pages.dev","topics":["application-framework","cpp","cross-platform","embeddable","ffi","http-server","lua","lua-scripting","runtime","scripting-engine","web-framework","webassembly","websocket"],"demo":"https://varn.pages.dev/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:47.637Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:47.637Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:47.637Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T14:48:39.092Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T16:42:03.731Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-13T02:09:53.693Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-19T02:46:47.637Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Lua everywhere. Write the whole application once in Lua and run that same code on a computer, a phone, or in the browser. Underneath it is a fast C++ core that already carries what a real product needs — a web layer, networking, background work, storage, data protection, and packaging — so there is nothing to assemble and nothing that behaves differently on the next device.","Lua is small enough to learn in an afternoon and expressive enough to hold a whole product, and the engine is what turns it from a scripting language into a place you can actually ship from.","Try it in your browser at varn.pages.dev — a playground running the real engine compiled to WebAssembly."],"features":["Every module is independent and used through require, so you pull in only what a script needs.","Full feature reference: docs/lua-api.md."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/varn-